<title>UK: Norwich says members' offer raised.</title>
<headline>Norwich says members' offer raised.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>British mutual insurer Norwich Union said on Thursday due to strong demand the members' offer in next week's flotation had been increased to 1.2 billion pounds ($2 billion).</p>
<p>That represents a clawback of 400 million pounds from the public offer. Norwich shares worth 800 million pounds had originally been reserved to meet applications from members.</p>
</text>
